# Specs — {{ project_name }}

One markdown file per domain. Each file is the source of truth for what must be tested
in that domain.

## How to create a new spec

1. Create `specs/<domain>.md`
2. Add the header (copy the template below)
3. Add one row per feature — status ❌ initially
4. Update status to ✅ when the test is written and passing
5. Add a row to `COVERAGE.md` for the new domain
6. Run `python scripts/coverage_report.py` to recompute totals

## Template

```markdown
# <Domain> — Test Spec

| Feature | Status | Test file | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Feature A | ❌ | — | AC from TICKET-1 |
| Feature B | ✅ | tests/domain/test_feature_b.py | Automated in TICKET-2 |
| Feature C | ⚠️ | tests/domain/test_feature_c.py | Partial — missing edge case |
```

## Status values

| Icon | Meaning |
|---|---|
| ✅ | Automated and passing |
| ❌ | Manual only — not yet automated |
| ⚠️ | Partial — test exists but coverage is incomplete |

## Rules

- Every row in a spec must be traceable to an acceptance criterion or ticket
- Never add a ✅ before the test passes in CI
- Never delete a ❌ row — it is deliberate coverage debt; mark it, don't hide it
- Run `python scripts/coverage_report.py` after every status change — keep COVERAGE.md in sync
